/-! Composed prepared O0 call, let, build and ordered-match contracts. Successful
source steps have concrete administrative GSLT paths; positive pattern
publications reflect to source bindings, and settled normalized searches
authorize source faults. Cached failure rows support ordered fallthrough
and exhaustive match failure. Provider-query firings reflect to encoded,
source-authorized cache answers. Every enabled administrative firing preserves its source control point
and lowers its rank. The declaration family, nested result variant and
pattern index are recovered from the actual firing. Every firing from an ordinary state with a successful independent source step
enters its successor control point; all instruction and return-frame cases
are covered. Finite source-result preservation now composes across runner prefixes and
provider restarts. Every control point of a finite independent source run
can step, request a source-authorized service, or expose its terminal result.
Settled pattern failures cover every retained occurrence, including duplicates.
Finite source evaluations admit no infinite committed transition sequence,
and every prepared search has a finite completion bound. Service and actual
controller liveness are connected in the downstream execution bridge.
-/
